    "durationMs": 341956,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Setup** — Created a Laravel 11 project with Composer (in `/tmp`, moved into `/workspace` which already had `.git`), dependencies installed. No `.env` file exists, so the provided `DB_*` environment variables are authoritative; `start.sh` uses `php artisan serve --no-reload` to keep them flowing to the server process.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `bootstrap/app.php` — registers `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are exactly `/links` and `/r/{code}` (no `/api` prefix), no throttle middleware on the group.\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — all endpoints return exact JSON shapes (`{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\"}`), with raw `getContent()` decoding so malformed JSON bodies reliably yield `422 {\"error\": ...}`. URLs are validated as absolute http/https with a host via `parse_url`, and returned byte-for-byte unchanged (responses use `JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES`). Codes are validated against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`; generated codes are 8 random chars with uniqueness retry. Duplicates return `409` (existence check plus a `1062` unique-violation catch for races). Redirects use an atomic `increment('clicks')` for exactly-once counting.\n- Migration — `links` table with unique `code` column pinned to `utf8mb4_bin` for exact-string (case-sensitive) code semantics.\n- `start.sh` — `php artisan migrate --force` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README has the start instructions.\n\n**Verified** — a 43-check curl suite plus dedicated tests, all passing on a fresh database created by `sh start.sh` itself: 201/409/404/422 paths, exact response bodies, Location header equality, exactly-once click increments, ascending list order with matching `total`, case-variant codes distinct, and data + click counts surviving a full server restart (migrations idempotent on re-run). Database left pristine with migrations applied."
